<<~ kanawai uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/ref/RFC-2119`>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! The island host contract

''The host shapes the island; the engine never sniffs it.'' Two laws hold the shore between a host and the TW5 engine it boots inside an island. The golden principle names the contracts the host reproduces and the authorities it withholds; `packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-host-bridge.ts` enacts it today. The SES gate names the boundary unpinned code waits on; that boundary rests on the road.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/golden-principle`>>

!! The golden principle

''The island reproduces the engine's expected contracts and denies the authorities it should not hold, so platform detection becomes a decision the host makes and never a sniff the engine does.''

* ''One boot flow, a small shore.'' `loadTiddlyWikiFromBlob` evaluates the core for every runtime. A `HeadlessBootEnv` carries the three pieces that differ (`resolveBuiltin`, `preSeedTw`, `processArg`), and `prepareHostBootInstance` picks the runtime; the rest of the flow stays platform-blind. The Node env hands back real builtins from an allowlist, the browser Worker env synthesizes `vm`, `path` and `os` shims, both deny `fs`, and each refuses every other `require` by name. The canonical model's proven collapse (a core plus injected closures, never `if(platform)`) repeats here one level down.
* ''The host decides the platform.'' On both island paths (the Node `worker_thread` and the browser Worker) `configureIslandRuntime` sets `$tw.node` and `$tw.browser` both to null: the third runtime, neither browser nor node. TW5's own platform filter then skips the `["browser"]` and `["node"]` startup modules and runs the agnostic ones. The host stubs the two loaders the kernel calls regardless (`loadTiddlersBrowser`, `loadTiddlersNode`), passes `decryptEncryptedTiddlers` straight through, steers `initStartup` away from the node block with `readBrowserTiddlers`, seats `packageInfo.version` as the SHA-256 of the engine's own bytes so `extractVersionInfo` never reaches for `document`, lends `escapeCSS` as a pure capability in place of a faked `window.CSS`, and routes `utils.error` onto the alert rail in place of `process.exit`.
* ''Why never a faked-browser DOM.'' A fake `window` and `document` that answer to `$tw.browser` route boot into the browser block and inherit its footguns: the encrypted-store decrypt path, which reads `encryptedStoreArea` off the document and raises a password prompt, and the autoboot, which fires on evaluation wherever `$tw.browser` answers and `suppressBoot` stands unset. Every pre-seed carries `boot.suppressBoot`, so the core never boots itself on evaluation; the host calls `boot()` once its neutralization stands. Headless render goes to `$tw.fakeDocument`, the engine's own DOM-less document, which camera-mount and deletion-map already hold for Node, MCP and worker-side render.
* ''Runtime injection stays irreducible.'' The core arrives as content-addressed bytes in the `coreBlob`, evaluated through `new Function`, and no bundler or build-time transform reaches inside a blob evaluated that way. So the host shapes the engine at run time alone: the pre-seed before evaluation, the env's closures during it, and `configureIslandRuntime` after it, before `boot()`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/ses-gate`>>

!! The SES gate

''No unpinned code enters the island realm until a Compartment boundary holds it, because hash-pinning vouches for provenance and never for intent.''

* ''Soundness.'' Pinning holds sound if and only if the set of code the island evaluates equals the set the host hash-verified. Any evaluation path outside that set (a module tiddler, a plugin, an evaluated string) breaks the equality, and a pin on the core then vouches for nothing the island runs beside it.
* ''What stands.'' `verifyCoreBootBlob` checks the core blob's bytes against the SHA-256 the blob carries and refuses a mismatch before evaluation. A blob that carries no expected hash passes unchecked, so the core check vouches only where a pin rides along.
* ''What rests on the road.'' No Compartment boundary stands in the code: no SES `lockdown`, no `Compartment`, no `harden`. This gate names the boundary unpinned code waits on; it never claims the boundary stands built. Until one stands, code without a pin MUST NOT enter the island realm.
* ''Never vm2.'' The island MUST NOT take `vm2`, or any `vm`-context sandbox, as its boundary. Node's `vm` serves the engine's module loader and grants no isolation.

<<~/ahu>>

